From f0fbb1fedaed68be9d1134996cf2497233ecfd0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Enver Ikromov <owner@ph4ntom-rev.uz>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:10:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH v5 10/10] wifi: rtw89: restore channel after monitor restart
 on non-chanctx devices

rtw89_alloc_ieee80211_hw() disables native chanctx callbacks
(ops->assign_vif_chanctx = NULL) and relies on mac80211 chanctx
emulation via hw->conf.chandef and rtw89_ops_config() whenever
chip->support_chanctx_num == 0 or the loaded firmware lacks
SCAN_OFFLOAD or BEACON_FILTER (for example on RTL8852AE with firmware
0.13.36.2, where support_chanctx_num == 1 but BEACON_FILTER is absent).

When the last monitor interface is brought down or deleted,
rtw89_ops_stop() powers down the MAC/BB/RF and clears the RTW89_PHY_0
entity state while mac80211 retains local->hw.conf.chandef. When a
monitor interface is brought up again on the same channel,
rtw89_ops_start() sets RTW89_FLAG_POWERON without programming the
channel (so subsequent rtw89_leave_ips() calls return early), and
ieee80211_hw_conf_chan() omits IEEE80211_CONF_CHANGE_CHANNEL because
chandef is unchanged, leaving RX/TX silent until a manual channel
change.

In rtw89_ops_config(), when IEEE80211_CONF_CHANGE_MONITOR enables
IEEE80211_CONF_MONITOR on devices without assign_vif_chanctx and
RTW89_PHY_0 is not yet active, apply hw->conf.chandef and call
rtw89_set_channel(). When IEEE80211_CONF_CHANGE_CHANNEL has already
configured RTW89_PHY_0, the entity state check avoids redundant RF
calibration.

Signed-off-by: Enver Ikromov <owner@ph4ntom-rev.uz>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/mac80211.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/mac80211.c b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/mac80211.c
index 771e8c9..c022961 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/mac80211.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/mac80211.c
@@ -134,9 +134,19 @@ static int rtw89_ops_config(struct ieee80211_hw *hw, int radio_idx, u32 changed)
 	    !rtwdev->scanning)
 		rtw89_enter_ips(rtwdev);
 
-	if (changed & IEEE80211_CONF_CHANGE_MONITOR)
+	if (changed & IEEE80211_CONF_CHANGE_MONITOR) {
 		rtw89_physts_parsing_init(rtwdev);
 
+		if ((hw->conf.flags & IEEE80211_CONF_MONITOR) &&
+		    !rtwdev->ops->assign_vif_chanctx &&
+		    !rtw89_get_entity_state(rtwdev, RTW89_PHY_0) &&
+		    cfg80211_chandef_valid(&hw->conf.chandef)) {
+			rtw89_config_entity_chandef(rtwdev, RTW89_CHANCTX_0,
+						    &hw->conf.chandef);
+			rtw89_set_channel(rtwdev);
+		}
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
